Voice To Hebrish for Ubuntu
===========================

  /usr/bin/voice-to-hebrish         the app (window + tray)
  /usr/bin/voice-to-hebrish-model   model CLI: status | check | download [--replace]
  /usr/lib/voice-to-hebrish/        app code + bundled sherpa-onnx (not in Ubuntu)
  ~/.config/voice-to-hebrish/       config.json
  ~/.local/share/voice-to-hebrish/  downloaded model versions, state.json

The model (~660 MB) downloads on first launch. For the hotkey, join the input
group and log in again:  sudo usermod -aG input $USER
The bundled wheels match the python3 minor version the package was built for;
rebuild after Ubuntu moves python3 to a new minor version.
